{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 39, :comments ["<b>See now that I, I am He, etc.</b> He doubled the saying of 'אֲנִי אֲנִי' twice, corresponding to two categories of idolatry that we alluded to in the preceding verse. For the first He said 'אֲנִי' — meaning, and not another whom you consider to be a complete deity. And corresponding to the idolatry performed through an intermediary, He said 'אֲנִי הוּא' — meaning, I alone. And He concluded by saying 'וְאֵין אֱלֹהִים עִמָּדִי' — no intermediary between Me and the created beings." "<b>I deal death and I give life.</b> This is against the sect who say that the agent of evil is not the agent of good, and that there are two powers. Therefore He said 'אֲנִי אָמִית וַאֲחַיֶּה' — and not in this particular alone, but even in the particulars of the agents of evil, 'אֲנִי מָחַצְתִּי וַאֲנִי אֶרְפָּא'. And our Sages of blessed memory interpreted it (Pesachim 68a); let their words be examined there." "<b>And none delivers from My hand.</b> Meaning, that all the created beings will die, and therefore He was precise to say 'וְאֵין מִיָּדִי' — and He did not say 'וְאֵין מַצִּיל מִיָּדִי' (and there is no deliverer from My hand)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:21:42.908402736Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}